The gate passed on commit 2da2af4a. GPT-6.2 Sol and Astra, and any other gpt-6 model id without a preset, now go to OpenAI's Responses API, so tool calls work on Codex's current default model. The commit is titled "Part of #1060" because rows 1 (other model families), 2 and 4 of that ticket are still open.

This session: the previous run was cut off after committing, before the slow checks. I ran them now:
• cargo fmt -- --check: clean.
• cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings: clean.
• cargo test: exit 0, 48 test binaries, 7,695 tests passed, none failed.
• No NEUTERED marker is left in src/ or tests/, and the working tree is clean, so there was nothing new to commit.

What the commit does (from its body and the three comments already on #1060):
• Routing: these ids are now built with yoagent's ModelConfig::generic("openai", id), which chooses the endpoint itself. I didn't copy its classifier into yoyo.
• Before and after, against a local stub (127.0.0.1, never OpenAI's servers): gpt-6.2-sol, gpt-6.2-astra and a made-up gpt-6.3-sol moved from /v1/chat/completions to /v1/responses. gpt-6-sol and gpt-6.1-sol were already on Responses. gpt-5.5, o3 and gpt-4o are unchanged.
• gpt-5.x and o-series: left on Chat Completions on purpose. I haven't checked OpenAI's docs for those families yet, so row 1 stays open, and a test pins that.
• Warning fix found mid-task: after the switch, the warning that a model is running on guessed limits would have gone silent for exactly these new ids. The same commit fixes that in model_limits_note.rs.
• Older tests: a few expected these ids to use Chat Completions, which was the bug. They were changed, not deleted, and the commit lists each one.
• Known models: gpt-6.2-sol and gpt-6.2-astra are added to the known list, taken from OpenAI's GPT-6.2 guide. yoagent has no preset for them yet, so their real output limits aren't set and they still run on a guess, now with the warning shown.
• Docs: models.md now says that gpt-6 ids use the Responses API, and that a proxy serving only /chat/completions should use --provider custom.
• Positive control: breaking the new branch (marker counted) made the new wire tests fail; restoring it made them pass.

The size check printed 16 warnings, none fatal. Both files this task grew (agent_builder.rs, commands.rs) had their size entries updated in the commit.

One thing to watch: the harness may add its usual commit with the same title that only touches .yoyo/. The code and the full write-up are in 2da2af4a.
